# apps/web — Vite SPA on :3001
#
# There is deliberately almost nothing here. The app talks to the API at the
# relative path /api, so it needs no base URL at runtime and no secrets: it is a
# static bundle served to a browser, and anything put in a VITE_* variable is
# readable by anyone who opens devtools. Never put SERVICE_TOKEN, a database
# password, or any other credential in this file.
#
# In development Vite proxies /api to the Hono server (see vite.config.ts).
# In production the SPA is served from the same origin as the API, so /api
# resolves without a proxy at all — which is also what keeps the refresh cookie
# first-party and CORS out of the picture.

# Where the dev proxy forwards /api. Must match PORT in apps/backend/.env.local.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:7090
